  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Roast beetroot: Preheat the oven to 220C. Line an oven tray with baking paper. Peel the beetroot, then cut into 2cm-thick wedges (see Kitchen 101). Put on the lined tray and drizzle with 2 tsp olive oil. Season with salt and pepper and turn to coat. Roast, turning halfway, for 25 mins or until golden and tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/263550/photos/large/roast_beetroot-269fa0267f3c73f5566082b81b30f53f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook freekeh: Meanwhile, fill a medium saucepan three-quarters full with water and bring to the boil. Cook the freekeh, partially covered, for 15-18 mins until tender. Drain.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/263551/photos/large/cook_freekeh-0dd040828425cc259e43716ec42295fe.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook beans: Bring a small saucepan of water to the boil for the beans. Trim the beans, then halve on an angle. Cook for 2-3 mins until tender. Drain and rinse under cold water. Put the pistachios on an oven tray and roast for 3-4 mins until toasted. Cool slightly, then coarsely chop.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/263552/photos/large/cook_beans-c536b37134e0b1efb4f98987dbc88370.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make dressing: Juice the lime into a large bowl. Crush ½ garlic clove. Add the garlic, 2 tsp olive oil, 2 tsp red wine vinegar and 2 tsp honey to the bowl, season with salt and pepper and whisk to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/263553/photos/large/make_dressing-81d1544ad9ec44dc363e12980b06f325.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the freekeh, beans, spinach and beetroot to the dressing and toss to combine. Divide the salad among bowls. Crumble over the feta, scatter over the pistachios and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/263554/photos/large/serve_up-8bea242aa0b5260930a70627bbaeb0b2.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: Beetroot can be messy to prepare so, if you prefer, wear a pair of disposable gloves to prevent your hands from turning pink.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/263555/photos/large/kitchen_101-65c0444a8b627b119dfa6b7bffd237b6.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
